From: Robert Samuel White <rsw@rswfire.com>
Sent: Saturday, February 22, 2025 12:41 AM
To: BLISS Logan * OPRD <Logan.BLISS@oprd.oregon.gov>
Subject: Re: End of the Month (Friday 28th) Schedule Change

Logan,

I appreciate the attempt you made here, but I think it is caused by a misun=
derstanding.

That thing with Leaf? I think you learned the wrong thing from it. Our firs=
t exchange was natural. The next day it was clinical. It was unnatural. And=
 when I asked for clarity, he doubled down.

I was never upset with him. I just saw the change in behavior and felt it w=
as inauthentic. And I don't do inauthentic.

You can be real with me. I don't need to be managed.

If you need me to cover a shift, you know I'm the easiest person in the wor=
ld to ask. And I know you are just being thoughtful.

Sam

________________________________
From: BLISS Logan * OPRD <Logan.BLISS@oprd.oregon.gov<mailto:Logan.BLISS@op=
rd.oregon.gov>>
Sent: Friday, February 21, 2025 3:58:57 PM
To: Robert Samuel White <rsw@rswfire.com<mailto:rsw@rswfire.com>>
Subject: End of the Month (Friday 28th) Schedule Change


Hi there Sam, I hope you are doing well,



I wanted to get in touch with you about a potential shift swap on the 28th =
of this month.  I have David & Lisa heading out on the 28th and I had them =
scheduled for the evening shift that day.  I was hoping you would be able t=
o cover that 2-6pm shift for the day instead of the 10am - 2pm shift as the=
y would like to leave before it gets dark.  The evening shift on a Friday i=
s going to be busier than the morning shift most likely and it would work b=
etter for coverage and being available to campers who have any questions or=
 are needing firewood or ice etc.



